  "limitations": [
    "42 counts emitted nonzero-size defined STT_FUNC symbols in one CGU, not independently established source-function entities or the 425-function project. Optimization can clone/merge/eliminate symbols in general.",
    "Equality is post-compilation output observation; it proves neither that LLVM work was skipped nor that a future cache may safely omit optimization/emission.",
    "Only body bytes, selected binding/visibility/section flags and symbolic relocations relative to each function were compared. Absolute layout, target symbol values/sizes, constant/global payloads, module flags, target/pipeline options and cross-function optimization dependencies are not a complete proven product key.",
    "These two scalar objects have only .strtab/.text/.rela.text/.note.GNU-stack/.symtab plus null; no exercised unwind, debug, COMDAT/group or constant/global-data payload establishes general reuse safety.",
    "A reusable native product would need an explicit input/dependency contract plus complete native metadata/relocation/linkage handling and current Verify/target/ABI binding. Equal output cannot supply those proofs.",
    "Source provenance is the fixed formal manifest/build-binary association and per-row CGU2 object hashes; the object itself does not embed a compiler-source authenticity proof."
